  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Human Capital in Ethiopia&#x2019;s Jimma zone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Primary school students in the Jimma zone and the Ethiopian Federal Ministry of Education</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching main objective on Human Capital project is to demonstrate that the simultaneous application of PBF in the health and education sectors can help build Human Capital in one district in Jimma Zone (Oromia Region, Ethiopia). 

Short term objectives
1.	Improve the availability and accessibility of good quality, inclusive primary education.
2.	Strengthen the governance of the education system in this district, in synergy with the health system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The vision of the Ethiopian Education Sector Development Plan (ESDP) VI is &#x201C;Transforming society through harnessing the full potentials of learners to become productive citizens&#x201D; (ESDP VI, 2021). The philosophy of the Federal Ministry of Education (FMoE) roadmap hinges on the preparation of the young generation for the future by building their moral, cognitive, social, spiritual, physical, psychological and vocational attributes whilst also understanding that education is a public good which serves as a means for social harmony and development which will transform Ethiopia into a respectable member of the world (ESDP VI, 2021). Several strides have been made by the Ethiopian government and its partners in the education sector through development and setting up of policy frameworks which the education sector is based on, in addition to investments in construction and equipping of various schools, and training of the human resources across the country. However, more needs to be done to build and sustain an education system that is comparable to other world class standards. 

Cordaid is piloting Performance Based Financing (PBF) in the education sector in Shabee district of Jimma zone to support the Federal Ministry of Education (FMoE) in achievement of the goals set in the ESDP VI. Performance Based Financing (PBF) is a social financing mechanism used in the health, education and security and justice in various Low and Medium Income Countries (LMIC) across the globe. PBF has already been implemented in the health sector of the Jimma Zone since 2019 (in all 21 woredas) and will continue to run in parallel to this pilot project. Through the combined implementation of PBF in health and education in one woreda (Shabee), this project aims to build Human Capital and create synergy between the two sectors</narrative>
  </description>
